# ============================================================================
# Mimikin settings. Everything here is optional: the server starts without a .env file.
#
# Linux, macOS:  cp .env.example .env
# Windows:       copy .env.example .env
#
# Uncomment the lines you need. The values shown are the defaults or examples.
# With docker run, pass the file with --env-file .env. With docker compose it is read by itself.
# Do not put a comment on the same line as a value: docker run would take it as part of the value.
# .env holds your secrets and is not committed (see .gitignore). After a change: docker compose up -d
# ============================================================================

# --- Docker Compose ---------------------------------------------------------

# Port of the library on this machine. Inside the container it is always 3000.
# NAS systems usually keep port 80 for their own web page: take another one here.
# With docker run this is the first number of -p 80:3000 and needs no setting.
# HTTP_PORT=80

# Port of the games. It sets both the published port and what the page opens, so with compose one line is enough.
# With docker run -p 9000:3001 it has to be set by hand: -e GAME_PORT=9000. Inside the container it is always 3001.
# The port must be reachable the same way as the library (home network, Tailscale). See README, "Changing ports".
# GAME_PORT=8081

# Folder on this machine with the games, the database and the saves. Mounted into the container as /games.
# It must be on a local disk: the SQLite database does not work reliably on a network share (NFS, SMB).
# GAMES_HOST_DIR=./games

# Compose project name. By default compose takes the folder name. Set it only to run two installs on one machine;
# they then also need different ports and different AUTH_COOKIE_NAME values.
# COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=mimikin

# Optional services from docker-compose.yml, off until listed here. The library finds them by itself, no address needed.
#   libretranslate - your own game translator without limits (several GB of language models on disk, 2-4 GB of memory)
# COMPOSE_PROFILES=libretranslate

# Memory limit of that service.
# LIBRETRANSLATE_MEMORY=4g
# Languages LibreTranslate loads: only what your games and interface need.
# LT_LOAD_ONLY=en,ja,zh,ru,de

# --- Text on pictures (ocr service, docker compose only) --------------------

# Address of the service. Empty turns the feature off and hides it. To skip the service and its 1.09 GB image,
# see README, "Requirements". Set in docker-compose.yml; docker run has no such service unless you point this at one.
# OCR_URL=http://ocr:8000

# CPU cores one picture takes, cores and memory for the whole service.
# OCR_THREADS=2
# OCR_CPUS=2
# OCR_MEMORY=2g

# --- Server -----------------------------------------------------------------

# Port the server listens on inside the container. Leave it: the compose health check and port mapping expect 3000.
# PORT=3000

# Key that signs logins. Without it the server creates one and keeps it in the database, which is enough for most people.
# Your own key: openssl rand -hex 64 (Windows: see README, "Windows").
# SESSION_SECRET=

# Name of the login cookie. Cookies ignore ports, so two installs on one host need different names,
# otherwise signing in to one signs you out of the other.
# AUTH_COOKIE_NAME=auth_token

# Redis address, used as a cache: the games list, site answers and the daily ScraperAPI counter. docker-compose.yml starts
# its own and points here by itself. The image alone (docker run) keeps all this in memory, so the counter starts over after
# a restart. Set this only for a Redis of your own: a Redis that is not there
# fills the log with errors.
# REDIS_URL=redis://redis:6379

# API requests a minute from one address. Raised by the interface tests.
# API_RATE_LIMIT=200

# 1 - the server goes to no website: no data lookup, no update checks, no site feeds on the home page and in the Find tab.
# For tests and the demo library.
# OFFLINE=1

# --- Paths (worked out from GAMES_DIR, normally left alone) -----------------

# GAMES_DIR=/games
# SAVES_DIR=/games/_saves
# EXTRACT_TMP=/games/_tmp_uploads
# AUDIOCACHE=/games/.audio-cache
# OLD_DIR=/games/_old
# TRASH_DIR=/games/_trash

# The inbox: an archive put here joins the library by itself. On another disk, mount that folder into the container too.
# INBOX_DIR=/games/_inbox

# --- Game lookup ------------------------------------------------------------

# ScraperAPI key (1000 free credits a month): the server opens itch.io pages through it, since the site's protection
# blocks direct requests. Without a key itch.io pages are not read; VNDB and Steam work anyway. An itch.io page costs 10 credits.
# Can also be set in the library: ... > Settings > Sources > ScraperAPI.
# SCRAPER_API_KEY=

# Daily ceiling for ScraperAPI, in credits. 1000 a month is about 33 a day, so one heavy day
# (looking up the whole library, browsing itch.io) cannot eat the month.
# Can also be set in Settings > Sources > ScraperAPI.
# SCRAPER_DAILY_LIMIT=30

# Optional services from docker-compose.yml, off until listed here. The library finds them by itself, no address needed.
#   libretranslate - your own game translator without limits (several GB of language models on disk, 2-4 GB of memory)
# After a change: docker compose up -d
# COMPOSE_PROFILES=libretranslate

# --- Game translation -------------------------------------------------------

# Translation service keys. Can also be set in Settings > Translation. Secrets.
# DEEPL_API_KEY=
# Microsoft: key|region
# MS_TRANSLATOR_KEY=
# GOOGLE_TRANSLATE_KEY=
# A LibreTranslate of your own: address|key. Not needed with COMPOSE_PROFILES=libretranslate.
# LIBRETRANSLATE_URL=

# --- Games on their own address ---------------------------------------------

# off - games run the old way, on the library's address, with access to everything. Only if games in a frame
# do not run on some device.
# GAME_ISOLATION=off

# --- Behind a reverse proxy (nginx, Caddy, Traefik) -------------------------
# Full examples: README, "Reverse proxy and HTTPS".

# How many proxies stand in front of the server. With it the server sees each visitor's real address (login and API limits
# are per address) and knows the login came over HTTPS (the login cookie gets Secure). Proxy addresses work too:
# 10.0.0.0/8, loopback, comma separated. Off by default. true trusts any X-Forwarded-For, which a visitor can forge.
# Without a proxy leave it off. With one, close direct access to the container ports, for example by publishing them on 127.0.0.1.
# TRUST_PROXY=1

# Full address of the games when it is not "the same host, port GAME_PORT". Behind HTTPS the games need their own address
# with TLS: a separate name (preferably on the same domain) or the same host with another port. The proxy sends it to
# container port 3001 and the library to 3000. Games cannot share the library's address: their code would get its login.
# Subfolders (/mimikin/) are not supported. A value that is not an http(s) address is ignored with a line in the log.
# GAME_ORIGIN=https://games.example.com

# --- Telegram ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Token of your own bot: in Telegram open @BotFather and send /newbot. Can also be set in Settings > Notifications.
# Then press Connect in Settings > Notifications. The bot sends finished uploads, a daily backup of the database and
# saves, and server problems. A secret: the token writes as your bot.
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=

# Chat to write to, if you do not want to connect it from the library. Usually empty.
# TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# Password for the backup sent to Telegram: with it the backup is a 7z with contents and file names locked, without it
# a plain zip. Forget it and the backup is useless. Can also be set in Settings > Backups.
# BACKUP_PASSWORD=

# Free disk space, in GB, below which a warning comes. Can also be set in Settings > Notifications.
# DISK_WARN_GB=10

# --- Downloads --------------------------------------------------------------

# Both are normally set in Settings > Downloads, and that is the better place: there the MyJDownloader password is turned
# into the two hashes its protocol signs in with and is not kept, and the seedbox gets an SSH key of its own.
# Here they are JSON on one line, and they win over Settings.
# MYJD_LOGIN={"email":"you@example.com","password":"...","device":"server","folder":""}
# SEEDBOX_LOGIN={"host":"seedbox.example.com","port":22,"user":"you","folder":"downloads","key":"...","hostKey":"..."}

# --- Picture analysis -------------------------------------------------------

# Background analysis of game pictures for picture search, the feed and picture tags. Downloads models once (740 MB).
# On by default (1), but it does not start by itself with less than 2 GB of memory. This is only the default:
# the switch in Settings > General > Picture analysis wins over it, both ways, and needs no restart.
# The image also sets MALLOC_MMAP_THRESHOLD_=131072 so closed models give their memory back; nothing to change there.
# PICTURE_PASS=1

# How much of the computer the analysis takes: quiet (default) - about one CPU core, the computer runs cooler, takes longer;
# fast - up to three cores, one and a half to two times faster, the computer can get hot. Only the default: the choice in Settings wins over it.
# PICTURE_SPEED=quiet

# 0 - no models at all: nothing is downloaded and picture search has nothing to work with. Made for tests; use the switch.
# GALLERY_VISION=0

# --- Keys and passwords -----------------------------------------------------

# Service keys, the bot token, the backup password and the MyJDownloader sign-in entered in Settings are
# stored encrypted in library.db. This is the encryption key: any long random string (openssl rand -hex 32).
# Not set: the server makes a random one in games/_media/.secrets.key, so the database copied without that file gives
# nothing away, but the whole folder does. Set here, it lives outside the games folder, which is safer.
# Change or lose it and saved keys have to be entered again; games, saves and the database stay.
# SECRETS_KEY=

# Where that key file lives, if not in games/_media/.
# SECRETS_KEY_FILE=/run/secrets/mimikin.key

# --- Updates ----------------------------------------------------------------

# Settings > About asks GitHub for a new version every 6 hours. 0 - do not ask. Can also be set there.
# UPDATE_CHECK=1

# Repository asked for new versions, if you run your own fork.
# UPDATE_REPO=your-name/your-fork

# The Update button: an update helper next to the container (Watchtower in HTTP API mode or compatible), the address of its
# /v1/update and its key. Without them there is a terminal command instead of the button. Can also be set in Settings > About.
# How to run the helper: README, "Updating".
# UPDATE_URL=http://mimikin-update:8080/v1/update
# UPDATE_TOKEN=

# --- Development only (docker-compose.dev.yml) ------------------------------

# Login of an existing user for the game compatibility check, which opens every game in turn:
# docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.dev.yml run --rm compat
# COMPAT_USER=
# COMPAT_PASS=

# Folder mounted read-only at the same path, for dev games linked with scripts/dev-link-games.sh.
# PROD_GAMES_DIR=
